  "created_at": "2025-02-04T06:38:29Z",
  "updated_at": "2025-02-04T06:38:29Z",
  "body": "> I believe that your implementation allocates a static area that needs to be at least as large as every shared library (with tls) before it loads the initial-exec tls shared libraries\n\nIt should be the first #TLS_STATIC_RESERVE_COUNT (16) dynamic libraries using TLS + anything that is statically linked that uses TLS. Regardless of them being TLS dynamic or initial-exec.\nSo, you could obviously run into that limitation, but at least this prints an error of what went wrong. I also haven't run into that in the wild yet, so it seems good for now?\n\n> Also, lib1,2,3 will be using the new area installed by install_new_tls\n\nYes.\n\n> So we are wasting a few hundred bytes in the static area?\n\nYes, a few KB. Generally I only see a couple 100 bytes being used.\n\n> I've been thinking about a more complete solution where the static area is tracked separately and only used on dlopening initial-exec tls libraries. It might be overengineered because it seems like shared libraries don't often use a lot of TLS, but still - could be nice to have a full solution!\n\nI wanted to do this as well at first, but debugging any of this is hell, so I kept it simple :)\nAnd if things go wrong, you might not immediately (or ever) notice or suspect this as the issue. I'd rather want it to fail loudly.",
  "author_association": "OWNER",
  "pin": null,
