  "updated_at": "2025-06-20T12:06:56Z",
  "body": "Sorry, but this is not really meant as a system level replacement, but rather for building your own static binaries. This also includes all dependent libraries you may need/want, as proper (direct) dynamic linking is currently broken, i.e. you can only use dynamic libraries by manually calling dlopen/dlsym/etc (with the exception that those may then use proper dynamic linking and pull in other .so files).\n\nAs far as what patches you need for CUDA specifically: I don't know, a lot, maybe all? It's also a moving target, as NVIDIA may decide at any point to use newer glibc functions or indirectly pull in libraries that need these.",
  "author_association": "OWNER",
  "pin": null,
