  "updated_at": "2025-06-20T16:43:20Z",
  "body": "That's only one of the required commits. You still need a lot of glibc compat on top of that.\nIt also depends on how much of CUDA you need. AFAIR getting the low-level CUDA driver to work (libcuda.so) is/was fairly simple, but as soon as you need any of the higher level libraries (or the Vulkan driver), you will need a lot more glibc compat and the TLS workaround. These also tend to pull in other GNU libraries that may or may not need replacement (e.g. I'm replacing libgcc_s.so with compiler-rt/libcxxabi/libunwind on my side).",
  "author_association": "OWNER",
  "pin": null,
